00:47:49.440 --> 00:47:55.520
they saw these men, these Vietnamese willing to just laying down their lives in droves.

00:47:56.560 --> 00:48:01.200
And they said, how are you ever going to conquer that? They're coming out of the woods. They're

00:48:01.200 --> 00:48:06.160
willing to die for their country. They're fighting for what they believe is their freedom.

00:48:06.960 --> 00:48:11.280
They wouldn't want a foreign country running their country any more than we would.

00:48:12.080 --> 00:48:19.920
Well, my uncle had resisted all of his advisors. We're telling him, you got to send 250,000 combat

00:48:19.920 --> 00:48:25.680
troops in. And he kept saying, no, no, no. In the end, he sent 16,000 advisors who weren't legally

00:48:25.680 --> 00:48:31.600
allowed to fight. They were green berets, but he would, he never sent a single combat troop.

00:48:31.600 --> 00:48:38.640
He resisted literally every single person around him. And Ellsberg went to interview my father.

00:48:38.640 --> 00:48:44.480
