00:48:44.480 --> 00:48:50.720
to him kind of the generic reasons why they didn't think it was right to go in. And then he said,

00:48:50.720 --> 00:48:56.560
but how did you know back then? How were you so prescient to know? And he said, my dad slapped

00:48:56.560 --> 00:49:02.160
his hand on the table and it went whack. And he said, it was just a resounding. And he said,

00:49:02.160 --> 00:49:08.320
because we were there, we saw that they were willing to die and that they didn't care,

00:49:08.320 --> 00:49:13.360
that it was, they were willing to sacrifice every single man, woman and child in their

00:49:13.360 --> 00:49:18.640
country for freedom. And we knew you could never beat that. Anyway, it was a beautiful story.

00:49:19.840 --> 00:49:25.840
That is a beautiful story. Dan is kind of the godfather of the whistleblower community.

00:49:26.400 --> 00:49:31.760
But we're all in close touch with the exception of Ed Snowden because it's just not

00:49:32.160 --> 00:49:39.200
it's not easy for Ed to stay in touch. But Tom Drake from NSA and Bill Binney and Kirk Webe from

